[attempt_10_rate_binding_diagnostic]
scope = "do_12 names approval/native_program.rs, but the explicit seven-path SCOPE and runner allowed list exclude it. Preserve that file and every condition; add production diagnostics at rpc_prepare_native_send's existing StagedNativeRateUse::stage error mapping in the allowed human_runtime.rs."
diagnostic = "The unchanged CarrierError is printed with disclosure binding, envelope/canonical and envelope/preparation digest equalities, actor, empty chain/windows, evidence count and head advance. Each authenticated proof reports actor, through_sequence versus prepared head, observed_core_ms versus constraint time, required and unique window, and common observed batch. The read-only StagedNativeRateAdvance::stage diagnostic reports its original error or remaining pending count without publishing anything."
proof = "assert_native_send_policy_history additionally requires observed_core_ms and observed_batch_id equal the independently acquired signed checkpoint timestamp and header hash; every existing first Prepare, restart, durable and wrong-identifier assertion remains unchanged."
constraint = "StagedNativeRateUse::stage computes SHA-256(prepared.canonical_bytes), the authorization envelope, and requires equality to both binding.canonical_digest and binding.preparation_id. verify_native_owner_send_purpose and inspect_native_send_capability require both binding values equal SHA-256(unsigned EVM call). If the diagnostic confirms those two unequal digests, no honest fixture window evidence can satisfy the condition; neither binding is substituted and no check is relaxed."
evidence = "Run hf-build then RUST_TEST_NOCAPTURE=1 hf-done; resolve their exact candidate revision, command, exit and private log through qualification.ledger. If the digest conflict is confirmed, this is an in-scope implementation blocked by an excluded production interface, not a fixture failure to disguise. This record precedes the final gates and claims no passing result."


